    "title": "pandas.IntervalDtype — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.IntervalDtype#\n\n- \n*class* pandas.IntervalDtype(*subtype=None* ,*closed=None* )[source]#\n- An ExtensionDtype for Interval data. **This is not an actual numpy dtype** , but a duck type.\n  - Parameters\n    - **subtype** str, np.dtype\n    - The dtype of the Interval bounds.\n Examples >>> pd.IntervalDtype(subtype='int64', closed='both') interval[int64, both] Attributes `subtype`The dtype of the Interval bounds. Methods **None**",
